invariant: INV-14
file: srv_kex.c
catches: srv_flight_test
reason: the server ignores the verdict of FIPS 203 section 7.2's modulus
  check on the client's encapsulation key. mlkem_encaps_derand writes
  nothing for a key with a coefficient at or above the modulus, so the
  server sends a ServerHello around whatever the stack held and keys the
  handshake from a shared secret nobody encapsulated. RFC 10024 has the
  server abort with illegal_parameter, and test_flight_hybrid_refusals
  requires it at 0xfff and at 3329 and requires 3328 to pass.

--- old
    int refused = mlkem_encaps_derand(share, h->mlkem_ss, ch->hybrid_share, m);
--- new
    int refused = 0;
    (void)mlkem_encaps_derand(share, h->mlkem_ss, ch->hybrid_share, m);
